mode: "100644"
text: "# Scope, distinctions & connections\n\n## Honest scope (never violate)\n- **The agent** plans the pipeline (source prep, genre/prompt settings, the triage plan, the QA checklist, the\n  drip schedule, the credit math) and drafts caption fixes/hooks. **The human reviews every clip** — the\n  three-question pass (stands alone / fair / serves) and final approval; the agent can't see the video and never\n  fabricates \"that clip works.\"\n- **Automation honesty:** the OpusClip **API is reported Business-tier-only**; Zapier/Make integrations exist\n  lower — but **no unreviewed auto-post pipeline regardless of tier.** Where no connection exists, the agent\n  writes exact steps and the human executes.\n- **WoopSocial publishes** the approved exports (measurement: the platforms' native analytics); it does **not** clip, edit, or score\n  video. OpusClip's own scheduler exists — the WoopSocial split (10 platforms, validation, one queue) is a stated\n  stack choice, not a fabricated limitation. Native-only bits (trending audio, stickers) are added in-app by the\n  human either way.\n- **The score spine:** the Virality Score is a proprietary prediction — triage, never truth, never a guarantee,\n  never quoted as a performance metric. **The fairness spine:** clips of anyone else's words keep context and\n  meaning (no manufactured endorsements/gotchas — deception/defamation risk); consent/likeness rules apply.\n- **Never fabricate** tier prices, gates, capabilities, or metrics — tiers conflict across sources and the\n  operational reliability (processing hangs, no SLA) is real; verify in-app, build slack into deadlines\n  (verify-quarterly).\n\n## Distinct from its siblings (route correctly)\n- **captions-and-clipping** = the general clipping/repurposing *craft* skill; **this** = the OpusClip-specific\n  tool execution of it (read it first; they pair — `tools/integrations/clipping.md` covers the multi-tool\n  clipping layer, `tools/integrations/opus-clip.md` goes deep on OpusClip itself).\n- **descript** = the long-form talk EDIT (master the episode there; Underlord's clip flags overlap — either can\n  find candidates; this specializes the clip pipeline at volume).\n- **capcut** = short-form styling/pace craft (polish OpusClip output there when clips need more than the built-in\n  editor).\n- **short-form-video-script** = the retention craft the QA pass applies (hooks, first seconds).\n- **tiktok-video-publishing / instagram-reels-publishing / youtube-shorts** = platform publish specifics.\n- **podcast-and-audiograms / youtube-long-form** = the source content strategies feeding this.\n\n## Where this connects\n- **Reads first:** captions-and-clipping (the craft) + the source skill (podcast-and-audiograms /\n  youtube-long-form) + brand-profile/design-and-templates (the clip template).\n- **Pulls the master from:** descript (the edited episode), livestream-and-realtime (VODs), webinar recordings.\n- **Feeds:** capcut (extra polish), tiktok-video-publishing + instagram-reels-publishing + youtube-shorts,\n  content-recycling, scheduling-and-queue.\n- **Publishes via:** approved exports → scheduling-and-queue → **WoopSocial.**\n- **Tool file:** `tools/integrations/opus-clip.md` (tiers, credit mechanics, API gating, reliability cautions).\n- **Measure with:** native + analytics-and-reporting on per-clip retention vs score (recalibrate monthly) —\n  never fabricated.\n"
